 ## Current positioning
 
+The AUA/GURS/SUFU 2024 guideline describes ATOMS as approved in Europe and Canada and under FDA review. It is used in Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.<sup>[[30]](#ref30)</sup>
+
 ATOMS is an adjustable, minimally invasive device that has been used for mild-to-severe post-prostatectomy SUI in primary and salvage settings. The AUA/GURS/SUFU 2024 guideline states that new evidence shows ATOMS is safe and effective in men with mild to severe SUI, and that men with prior radiotherapy or prior urethral stricture surgery had significantly worse continence, complication and satisfaction outcomes. The AUA/GURS/SUFU guideline advises against routinely implanting male slings in severe SUI (Moderate Recommendation) and recommends an AUS over a sling or adjustable balloon after radiotherapy (Moderate Recommendation).<sup>[[30]](#ref30)</sup> The EAU 2026 guideline rates evidence for adjustable slings as limited (level 3) and makes no recommendation for their use because evidence for added benefit from adjustability is absent.<sup>[[35]](#ref35)</sup> Reported advantages:
 
 - **Postoperative adjustability.** Adjustment is done in clinic through the SSP without reoperation.<sup>[[6]](#ref6)[[11]](#ref11)</sup>
