 ## Perineorrhaphy in Obstetric Perineal Repair
 
-Reconstruction of the perineal body is also part of obstetric laceration repair when a second-degree or deeper tear disrupts it. That immediate postpartum repair is a different population and operation from elective POP perineorrhaphy. Obstetric guidance describes reapproximation of the bulbospongiosus and transverse perineal muscles after vaginal-mucosal closure. For episiotomy or second-degree tear repair, continuous suturing reduces short-term pain compared with interrupted suturing; when a suitable wound permits it, leaving the skin unsutured can reduce pain at 3 months. These obstetric perineal-repair findings cannot be applied to elective prolapse surgery.<sup>[[16]](#ref16)[[24]](#ref24)</sup>
